!!! info "Product Overview"
    **VIEWE 8-inch Transflective TFT Display** is a high-resolution (1200*1920 FHD) portrait screen engineered for demanding outdoor environments. By utilizing **Transflective technology**, it natively reflects ambient sunlight to provide superior readability without relying heavily on the backlight, achieving **extreme low-power consumption** under direct sunlight. Equipped with a responsive capacitive touch panel, it is the ideal choice for outdoor handheld terminals, rugged industrial tablets, and marine navigation equipment.

---

## 1. Key Features

Here are the main technical specifications for the 8-inch high-resolution display:

*   **Display Technology**: Transflective TFT-LCD (Excellent sunlight readability & power saving).
*   **Screen Size**: 8.0 inch (Diagonal).
*   **High Resolution**: 1200 x 1920 Pixels (Portrait orientation).
*   **Interface Type**: MIPI DSI (High-speed differential signaling).
*   **Touch Panel**: Capacitive Touch Screen (Multi-touch support via I2C interface).
*   **Optical Performance**: 
    *   *Transmissive Mode*: Active backlight for indoor/dark environments.
    *   *Reflective Mode*: Uses ambient light outdoors, reducing backlight power up to 80%.

---

## 2. Pinout Definition

The module connects via a high-density FPC connector. Below is the hardware pinout description for the display and touch panel interfaces:

### Main MIPI & Power Interface

| Pin No. | Symbol | I/O | Description |
| :---: | :--- | :---: | :--- |
| 1 | **VCI** | P | Analog Power Supply (3.3V) |
| 2 | **VDDI** | P | Interface I/O Digital Power Supply (1.8V) |
| 3 | **GND** | G | System Ground |
| 4 | **MIPI_D0_P** | I/O | MIPI DSI Data Lane 0 (Positive) |
| 5 | **MIPI_D0_N** | I/O | MIPI DSI Data Lane 0 (Negative) |
| 6 | **GND** | G | System Ground |
| 7 | **MIPI_CLK_P** | I | MIPI DSI Clock Lane (Positive) |
| 8 | **MIPI_CLK_N** | I | MIPI DSI Clock Lane (Negative) |
| 9 | **RESET** | I | Global Hardware Reset Pin (Active Low) |
| 10 | **LEDK** | P | LED Backlight Cathode (Negative) |
| 11 | **LEDA** | P | LED Backlight Anode (Positive) |

### Capacitive Touch Panel (CTP) Interface

| Pin No. | Symbol | I/O | Description |
| :---: | :--- | :---: | :--- |
| 1 | **CTP_VDD** | P | Touch Panel Power Supply (3.3V) |
| 2 | **CTP_SCL** | I | I2C Clock Line (Requires External Pull-up) |
| 3 | **CTP_SDA** | I/O | I2C Data Line (Requires External Pull-up) |
| 4 | **CTP_INT** | O | Interrupt Output Pin to Host MCU/CPU |
| 5 | **CTP_RST** | I | Touch Panel Reset Pin (Active Low) |

---

## 3. Reference Initialization Code

Since this high-resolution screen uses a **MIPI DSI** interface, it is typically driven by an ARM Cortex-A Linux/Android SoC (e.g., Rockchip, NXP i.MX, or Raspberry Pi Compute Module). Below is a reference initialization sequences for the display panel IC register setup:

```c
// VIEWE 8" 1200x1920 Transflective TFT Driver Initial Code
void VIEWE_8inch_MIPI_Init(void) 
{
    // 1. Hardware Reset Sequence
    LCD_RESET_HIGH();
    delay_ms(10);
    LCD_RESET_LOW();
    delay_ms(20);
    LCD_RESET_HIGH();
    delay_ms(50);

    // 2. Exit Sleep Mode
    MIPI_DSI_Write_Cmd(0x11); 
    delay_ms(120);

    // 3. Power Control & Panel Timing Settings (Optimized for Transflective)
    MIPI_DSI_Write_Reg(0xB1, 0x01, 0x1C, 0x1C); 
    MIPI_DSI_Write_Reg(0xC0, 0xA2, 0x02, 0x84); 
    
    // 4. Resolution & Lane Configuration (1200x1920 Portrait)
    MIPI_DSI_Write_Reg(0xD6, 0x01); // Set 4-Lane MIPI Mode
    
    // 5. Display On
    MIPI_DSI_Write_Cmd(0x29); 
    delay_ms(20);
}